    description: "Rust: an explicit receiver self: &Self hashes differently from &self, two spellings of one receiver.\n\nREPRO (PR 3 branch, commit 4e0163454): normalize_rust_signature(\"(self: &Self)\") != normalize_rust_signature(\"(&self)\"). That commit writes &self as self: &Self and &mut self as self: &mut Self so the receivers stop colliding; the explicit long form is not mapped to the same text. Evidence: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/tojov/RESULTS.md residual 3. Not measured: how often the explicit form appears in real trees."  # eb9e
